WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:05.300
Hey YouTubers, it's Charlie!  So, a lot of you guys
requested an Arthur Dayne video,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.800
so this is going to be a little bit of
the history of House Dayne,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.840
but mostly focusing on Arthur Dayne's life
up to Robert's Rebellion.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.380
He's not a character that's alive
on the show right now,

00:00:14.385 --> 00:00:17.052
and we haven't even really seen that much
from House Dayne,

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.520
but he's just one of those characters
that ties a lot of things together --

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.660
a lot of historical events and a lot of stuff that's going on in present day.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.040
So there's hope that the TV show
might do his character in some way.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.280
Most of the times when we hear about him,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.800
it's when characters are
talking about him in past tense,

00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:34.440
like Catelyn Stark or Jaime Lannister.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.160
Jaime Lannister almost worships
the ground that he walked on,

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:41.287
because when he first joined the Kingsguard,
Arthur Dayne was the one who taught him to fight.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.420
So Jaime Lannister was like one of
the best swordsmen in the realm,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.980
you know, before he lost his sword hand,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.960
then Arthur Dayne is that much better.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.400
So not only does the fandom hype him up,

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.680
other characters inside the narrative hype him up.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.100
But just going back into the history of House Dayne first,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.620
just to add some context --

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.620
The legend goes that 10.000 years ago,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.907
a First Man, the creator of House Dayne,

00:01:03.907 --> 00:01:07.087
saw a meteor fall to earth near the Torrentine river here,

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.680
used it to forge their ancestral blade called Dawn,

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.780
and built Starfall, their ancestral home on the site.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.440
Their family ruled over that area for thousands of years

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.879
until Nymeria's war, about 700 BC.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.213
That's the 10.000 ships

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:24.713
when Queen Nymeria brought her people and conquered Dorne.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.900
House Dayne was defeated and thereafter
they were bound to service to the Martells

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:33.260
For history buffs, Queen Nymeria took a Dayne for her third husband,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.736
But the reason that House Martell went on to rule Dorne

00:01:36.736 --> 00:01:40.816
is because her oldest daughter succeded her,
and she was born of a Martell.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.738
But even though the Daynes are
bannermen to House Martell

00:01:43.738 --> 00:01:45.698
they're still a legendary House.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.180
They go all the way back to the First Men,

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.080
all the way back to the building of the Wall.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.880
Because of that, they actually look like
the rest of the people in Westeros,

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.440
just very pale-skinned.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.660
The show always plays it fast and loose
with the way characters look,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.040
depending on which area they're from,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.060
but the Rhoynish people generally look like this.

00:02:02.462 --> 00:02:05.702
Really the biggest thing that people talk about,
when they talk about Arthur Dayne,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.760
is his sword.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.600
His title is "Sword of the Morning".

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.680
It's part of their family's tradition,
that they pass their sword down

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.080
to the most worthy person.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.460
It's a lot like Thor's hammer.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.740
"Let he who be worthy wield this blade."

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:20.240
Not a lot is known about the meteorite metal
that the blade is made of,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.560
only that it's just as strong as Valyrian Steel,

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.240
but it's a completely different metal.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.734
Currently in the story there's no one wielding the blade;
it just resides at their family's home at Starfall.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.820
Ned Stark took it there after Artur Dayne died
during Robert's rebellion.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.600
There are other Daynes that are alive right now,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.420
but no one is wielding it, because none of them
have been deemed worthy.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.040
Edric Dayne is the current Lord of the House,
but he's only about 12 years old.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.620
He's another character that we haven't seen
on the show yet,

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.040
but in the books he's part of the
Brotherhood Without Banners,

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.920
so if he would have been on the show, we would
have seen him whenever Arya ran into them.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.380
There are really two big events
in Arthur Dayne's life

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.780
that are significant to what's been going on
on the show so far.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.080
There's the Smiling Knight, which is
a big event in Jamie Lannister's personal history,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.720
and then there's the Tower of Joy,

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.860
which is a HUGE nexus for rumors, but is like
a big personal event in Ned Stark's history.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.840
The Smiling Knight is a really infamous outlaw
that Jamie calls the Mountain of his youth.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.880
So, when you think of the Smiling Knight,
just think of Franken-Mountain here.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:23.140
The knight was causing all kinds of trouble,
so the Kingsguard were ordered to put him down.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.940
You see how events in history
repeat themselves a little bit.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.140
So Jamie almost got his head squished like a grape,
just like Oberyn Martell did.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.720
Arthur Dayne rides in, saves him,
then defeats the Smiling Knight in the swordfight.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.351
So, when you picture Arthur Dayne,
think of someone so badass with a sword,

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.463
that they could take Franken-Mountain down.

00:03:40.463 --> 00:03:43.283
The Tower of Joy incident happened years after that.

00:03:43.283 --> 00:03:45.586
That was during Robert's Rebellion --
towards the end of that.

00:03:45.586 --> 00:03:49.459
So, as a Kingsguard, Arthur Dayne became
a really close personal friend --

00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:52.220
like THE closest friend --
of Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.260
So, regardless of Rhaegar's actions or his motives
for capturing Lyanna Stark,

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.800
Arthur followed him around,
protecting him everywhere.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.040
And when Rhaegar was called away
to lead the Mad King's forces at the Trident,

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:07.160
he left Arthur Dayne behind at the Tower of Joy
to protect Lyanna Stark.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.440
Ned Stark and Howland Reed found out
she was there, went to rescue her,

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:13.500
ended up killing Arthur Dayne --
Ned Stark killed Arthur Dayne --

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.419
and they found Lyanna dying,
surrounded by her own blood.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:21.860
This sequence of events sets the stage for
a lot of the Jon Snow's mother tin-foil theories.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.920
I've already done a video on Lyanna Stark,
so I'll put a link for it in the description,

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.200
if you want to learn more about that.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.480
But even though he ended up killing him,
Ned Stark still called Arthur Dayne

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.440
the finest knight that he ever knew.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.040
He was just a legendary knight
with a legendary sword.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:41.820
Currently, the TV show is trying to cast a character
for season six that meets his description.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.420
but that's not confirmed; like,
we don't know that they're doing Arthur Dayne.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.200
It just says that the actor they're looking for is
a legendary knight with a legendary sword.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:54.380
And in real life, the actor that they cast
needs to be AMAZING with a sword.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.660
So, presumably, whoever they cast is going to be
doing some really badass sword-fighting

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.360
with a really legendary sword.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.580
Whether or not it's in a flashback,
we have no idea.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.760
